<!-- FG_03. The two arms are laid out as two labelled bands because that is how the
     station is reasoned about: arm 2 picks out of slot 1, arm 1 places into
     slot 2, and the handover is the moment both grippers hold the part. Reading
     the seven cylinders as one undifferentiated grid loses that.

     Grid: columns at x = 20 / 290 / 560 / 830 / 1100 (260 wide, 270 pitch); a
     Cylinder tile is 260x250, a BinarySensor tile 260x120. A section label is 20
     tall and the band under it starts 26 lower, so the label breaks the row rhythm
     deliberately - it is not a tile. See FG_01.content for the full grid note.

     EACH GRIP SENSOR SITS IN ITS OWN ARM'S BAND, immediately after that arm's
     gripper, because that is the pairing that matters: the gripper tile says where
     the jaws are and the sensor tile says whether anything is between them, and the
     two disagree exactly when something has gone wrong. -->
<div id="FG03_Devices" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiContent" data-tchmi-top="0" data-tchmi-left="0" data-tchmi-width="100" data-tchmi-height="100" data-tchmi-width-unit="%" data-tchmi-height-unit="%">

<div id="FG03_Title" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.Beckhoff.TcHmiTextblock" data-tchmi-left="20" data-tchmi-left-unit="px" data-tchmi-top="12" data-tchmi-top-unit="px" data-tchmi-width="500" data-tchmi-width-unit="px" data-tchmi-height="26" data-tchmi-height-unit="px" data-tchmi-text="FG_03 - transfer and flip" class="headline-2">
</div>

<div id="FG03_Module" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiUserControlHost" data-tchmi-target-user-control="UserControls/PackML_BaseModul.usercontrol" data-tchmi-left="20" data-tchmi-left-unit="px" data-tchmi-top="48" data-tchmi-top-unit="px" data-tchmi-width="650" data-tchmi-width-unit="px" data-tchmi-height="25" data-tchmi-height-unit="px" data-tchmi-module="%s%ADS.PLC1.MAIN.Machine.FG_03.HMI%/s%">
</div>

<div id="FG03_Arm2Label" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.Beckhoff.TcHmiTextblock" data-tchmi-left="20" data-tchmi-left-unit="px" data-tchmi-top="413" data-tchmi-top-unit="px" data-tchmi-width="500" data-tchmi-width-unit="px" data-tchmi-height="20" data-tchmi-height-unit="px" data-tchmi-text="Arm 2 - picks out of slot 1">
</div>

